DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ttaaiill copies the last part of _f_i_l_e, or of the standard input
     if none is named, onto the standard output.  If no _n_u_m_b_e_r is
     given, the last ten lines are copied.

     The optional first argument is a + or - sign followed by a
     _n_u_m_b_e_r and, optionally, one of the letters bb, cc, or ll. A -
     sign (the default) counts _n_u_m_b_e_r backward from the end of
     the file; a + sign counts it forward from the beginning.
     The letter ll (the default) means _n_u_m_b_e_r is a count of lines;
     a scale of bb means 512-byte blocks and cc means characters
